{"text": "**This memo is confidential to the business of the company: it. should\nbe carefully handled, is not transferable to another individual, and is\nnot to be photocopied. **\nPOL MEMO 5236\nDATE: November 3, 1988\nPOL TEST NUMBER: 5236\n\nTITLE: POL 5236 - Newport 85mm vs HB-2 with 8611-21-1 A/C Application\nmm\n\nTEST REQUESTER: J. Hickle\nPOL STUDY LEADER: NM. Fleming\nPREPARED BY: J. Hall-Dabney\n\nPURPOSE: To determine consumer acceptability of MB-2 with 8611-21-1 A/C\nApplication II vs Newport 85mm\n\nPROCEDURE [BALLOT]: Sequential Monadic NV65SB\nSAMPLE SIZE: 1000 % RETURNED: 42\nSMOKER GROUPS:\n\nUsable Returns\n\nNewport 85mm 4\nKool 85mm a1\nSalem 85mm 113\n\nANALYTICAL SUMMARY: The MB-2 with 8611-21-1 A/C Application II 85mm\ncigarettes were different from the Newport 85nm cigarettes in porosity.\nBoth cigarettes were overtipped.\n\nCIGARETTES MADE: 8/31/88 CIGARETTES SHIPPED: 9/15/88\nDATA DATE: 10/27/88 .\nRESULTS DISCUSSED WITH REQUESTER [DATE]: 10/28/88\n\nRESULTS: There were significant differences between the cigarette ratings\nfor some snoker groups.\u201d The Newport smokers did not rate the cigarettes.\nsignificantly different on any of the scales. The Kool 85nm smokers rated\nthe Newport higher on amount, of unusual flavor. The Salem 85m smokers\nrated the Newport higher on harshness. They rated the NB-2 higher on\namount of menthol, satisfaction, cool smoking and liking.\n\nCOMMENTS: The MB-2 model evaluated in this POL was tested on MOOG in March.\n\nThis cigarette was positioned near Newport (between the Kool and Salem\nregions).* The model was not. significantly different from the 1987\nreplicates of the three competitive menthol brands (Newport, Kool, and\n\u2018alen) .\n\nPLANS: No additional testing of the MB-2 with Q611-21-1 is planned at this\n\u2018time.\n\n*H00G Memo, dated June 24, 1988, \"POL MEMO MOOG\".  @gg.99237\n\n068S8eS20z", "words": [{"text": "**This", "x0": 125, "y0": 100, "x1": 166, "y1": 110, "conf": 0.0}, {"text": 